.TH geectl-remote-delete-project 1  "geectl-remote-delete-project 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-remote\-delete\-project \- Delete a project. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the deletion. Without `\-\-recursive` a project holding packages is refused
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl remote delete\-project\fR [\fB\-\-recursive\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a project. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the deletion. Without `\-\-recursive` a project holding packages is refused
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-recursive\fR
Delete the project with all its packages
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Ignore other projects depending on this one
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR
A comment recorded on the delete
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to delete
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
